<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-SUPERCUP/CONMEBOL CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SUPERCUP/CONMEBOL CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of midweek games in</p>
<p>South American club competitions:</p>
<p>Supercup, first round, first leg</p>
<p>In Belo Horizonte, Brazil: Cruzeiro (Brazil) 3 Nacional</p>
<p>(Uruguay) 1 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Cruzeiro - Palhinha (20th, penalty), Paulinho (70th),</p>
<p>Fabinho (88th)</p>
<p>Nacional - Fernandez, own goal (55th)</p>
<p>Cruzeiro win 4-2 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Buenos Aires: Velez Sarsfield (Argentina) 1 Gremio</p>
<p>(Brazil) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Christian Bassedas (89th minute)</p>
<p>Attendance: 17,000</p>
<p>Velez Sarsfield win 4-3 on aggregate</p>
<p>Note: the Supercup is played every year between past winners</p>
<p>of the Libertadores Cup.</p>
<p>Conmebol Cup, first round, second leg:</p>
<p>In Rio de Janeiro: Fluminense (Brazil) 2 Guarany (Paraguay)</p>
<p>2 (0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Fluminense - Paulo Roberto (75th, penalty), Hugo (79th)</p>
<p>Guarany - Edgar Baez (27th), Aristides Rojas (34th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 2,328</p>
<p>Played Tuesday:</p>
<p>In Sao Paulo: Palmeiras (Brazil) 3 Bragantino (Brazil) 0</p>
<p>(2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Djalminha (31st), Viola (40th), Leonardo (67th)</p>
<p>Bragantino win 5-4 on aggregate</p>
</text>
